From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JohannaWeb <joaocordeiroalmeida@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Read text and comment nodes' layout as the shared default

`Node::layout_data` panicked ("`layout_data` is not available on this
node kind") for text and comment nodes, and so did every read accessor
built on it (`final_layout`, `unrounded_layout`, `scroll_offset`, ...).
Code that walks `children` reaches those nodes routinely: Aurora's
`document_height`, run on every wheel scroll, panicked on the first text
child. They have no box, so return the shared default layout (zero size
at the origin) that elements without layout output already get. Writes
through `layout_data_mut` still panic.

Still present on blitz main. Covered by
layout_queries_on_text_and_comment_nodes_do_not_panic in
src/blitz_document.rs.

diff --git a/src/node/node.rs b/src/node/node.rs
index 2dff68c..9d282f9 100644
--- a/src/node/node.rs
+++ b/src/node/node.rs
@@ -183,14 +183,16 @@ impl Node {
     /// This node's layout output state, or a shared default if layout has
     /// never written to this node.
     ///
-    /// Panics for node kinds which do not participate in layout (text and
-    /// comment nodes).
+    /// Node kinds which do not participate in layout (text and comment nodes)
+    /// have no box, so they read as the shared default (zero size at the
+    /// origin) rather than panicking: callers walking `children` (e.g. to
+    /// measure content height) reach them routinely.
     #[inline]
     pub fn layout_data(&self) -> &LayoutData {
         match &self.data {
             NodeData::Element(data) | NodeData::AnonymousBlock(data) => data.layout_data(),
             NodeData::Document(data) => data.layout_data(),
-            _ => panic!("`layout_data` is not available on this node kind"),
+            _ => &super::element::DEFAULT_LAYOUT_DATA,
         }
     }

